  "interpretation": {
    "changed_save": "Candidate remains slower than legacy: about +25.9% unprobed conventional median and +27.9% p95. Compared with pre-fix candidate 5df34d unprobed (median 587.831 ms, p95 660.726 ms), the serialization reuse candidate is about 12.1% faster at median and 15.8% at p95. Remaining changed-path cause is not isolated by this final run; earlier symmetric profile localized most measured difference to the save path, but its instrumentation point was pre-fix and inclusive phase timings are not additive.",
    "no_op_save": "Candidate is about 56.5% faster unprobed at median and avoids canonical/recovery writes; instrumented counters show one full read/hash per no-op save, with zero temp writes, backups, syncs, promotions, or journal removals.",
    "measurement_limits": "Unprobed latency has no filesystem/service counters. Instrumented baseline file-I/O counters have no service diagnostics; candidate service diagnostics provide full-read/hash/write counts. RSS, device physical write amplification, and in-process peak buffers are not measured."
  }
